<h1>coding tree</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="fullBinaryTree.html"><em>full binary tree</em></a> that represents a coding, such as produced by <a href="huffmanCoding.html"><em>Huffman coding</em></a>.  Each <a href="leaf.html"><em>leaf</em></a> is an encoded symbol.  The <a href="path.html"><em>path</em></a> from the <a href="root.html"><em>root</em></a> to a leaf is its codeword.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="fullBinaryTree.html"><em>full binary tree</em></a>, <a href="trie.html"><em>trie</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Aggregate parent</strong> (I am a part of or used in ...)<br>
<a href="huffmanCoding.html"><em>Huffman coding</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="prefixcode.html"><em>prefix code</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

